READY TO DEPLOY (merged into development, not on the server yet; dev1 deploys)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- dev3, PR #877 (#573): core only, no migration or setting. The Transcript Cleaner no
  longer merges a new name into a known look-alike. (1) With the known name in the same
  line, a look-alike word stays as heard ("Today Isolde heals the wounded, and Ysolde
  rests."). (2) A fix by sound is silent only when spelled at least 0.95 alike; closer
  than the old bars but below that it is made WITH a note and Undo in ✏️ Name fixes to
  check, and under Quiet it is not made. So **almost every fix by sound is now a note,
  not a silent fix** (also "Beleros" → Belleros): watch how many notes appear in a
  session. Same-letters respellings ("Kazeth" → "Ka'zeth") and the DM's own fixes stay
  silent. (3) A name the DM confirmed is never merged again. Check in the next
  names-stress test: Isolde and Rothgar next to Ysolde and Hrothgar stay as heard; a
  lone one is fixed but noted with Undo; real mishearings are still fixed. If the notes
  pile up, tell dev3: one constant (NEAR_CERTAIN) moves the line.
- dev2, PR #869 (#865): core with **migration 0031** (a new table `house_rules` and a new
  column `campaigns.house_rules_made`; the migration runs when core starts, so rebuild
  core). No setting. `/dmbot houserules`: a campaign's house rules, which everyone in the
  server can read and only the campaign's DMs can add, edit or remove. Each rule keeps its
  own number for good. Check, as the DM: the list says "No house rules yet" with an **Add a
  house rule** button; add two (a form with "The rule" and "Instead of (optional)") and the
  list shows "2." above "1." and "Each rule keeps its number, even when others are
  removed."; Remove 1 asks first, then says "Removed house rule 1." and sends the words to
  copy; add one more and it is **3**, not 1. As a player: the same list, no buttons. In the
  logs: migration 0031 applied, no error. The website's database role has no access to the
  table, so web-api needs nothing.
- dev2, PR #875 (#866): core only, no migration or setting. The rules index: DMbot now
  ships the System Reference Document 5.2.1's 339 spells and 15 conditions (CC-BY-4.0;
  the attribution is in the README and core/src/dmbot/rules/data/srd52/ATTRIBUTION.md)
  and can look them up by name, with a citation. Nothing calls it yet (the rules advisor
  will), so there is nothing to see in Discord. Check: core starts after the rebuild and
  logs no error. For dev1, once, after #889 merges (it changes a few line breaks in the
  data): download the official PDF (its address is in ATTRIBUTION.md) into a folder of its
  own and run `python -m dmbot.devtools.srd <the PDF>` from core/ in a checkout; `git diff`
  must show nothing.
- dev3, PR #872 (#399): core only, no migration or setting. The after-session name scan
  no longer suggests a word of a known name that was said whole ("Oskar" when Oskar Vane
  is known and "Oskar Vane" was said); a lone "Oskar" elsewhere is still suggested. Check
  after a session: "Check new names" doesn't offer the first word of a two-word name the
  campaign already has.
- dev2, PR #847 (#677): core only, no migration or setting. The DM can put back a line
  the off-topic filter left out by mistake. One DM-screen message per session, "🙈 Left
  out as off-topic", edited in place, with the newest 10 runs and a "Put it back N" button
  each; it shows at every level, quiet included. Needs the off-topic filter on (the AI key
  set). Check: say something plainly off-topic and then some game talk until a window is
  labelled; the DM screen lists the off-topic line with its button; Put it back replies
  "↩️ Put back N: <name>'s words are back…", the line reads "↩️ Put back: …", and the
  cleaned download (/transcript) shows the words, not "[…s of off-topic chat skipped]"; a
  player's press is refused ("Only this campaign's DM"); after /dmbot stop the buttons are
  gone and the message says "Session over". Core logs no ERROR.
- dev2, PR #804 (#771 part 1): free access. **Core, migration 0030 and web-api are live
  (23:36).** **Leave DMBOT_FREE_USERS empty until #806 (the account page for covered
