- CloudDev, PR #870 (#685) and PR #895 (#878): core only, no migration or setting. 📤
  Download all of a big campaign now comes as several files, each small enough to upload
  again with 📥 Add many > 📎 Upload a file (any order, a file twice does no harm); the
  message says how many files and messages. Each downloaded file's own header says how to
  add it back; if Discord refuses a later message, the DM is told which files didn't arrive
  and that the earlier ones are fine. Names with line separators are refused. Check: in a
  test campaign with a few thousand names, 📤 Download all gives several files named
  names-01-of-NN-..., uploading them one by one adds every name, and the header text in a
  file mentions "Add many > Upload a file".
- CloudDev, PR #879 (#164): core only, no migration or setting. Campaign backups are built
  piece by piece (less memory) and refuse, with a clear message, a copy too big to send in
  this server (a copy over 10 MB says it needs a boosted server or Nitro). Check: the
  backup of a normal campaign downloads and loads as before.
- CloudDev, PR #883 (#437 part 2a): core, **one migration (0032_usage, two tables:
  session_usage and owner_hours)**; deploying runs it. The hours meter only RECORDS how
  long DMbot listens (once a minute and at the stop); nothing is refused or warned yet, so
  nothing should look different at the table. Check: after migrating, start and stop a
  short session; the logs show no errors from the meter and the session_usage row (read
  only, as dmbot_ro, numbers only) holds about the minutes listened. Nothing from it goes
  in a report.

